bookmarks":122,"views":7683,"is_note_tweet":false,"replying_to":null,"quote":null,"media":null,"reposted_by":null},{"id":"2109376465150357569","url":"https://x.com/marcelkargul/status/2109376465150357569","author_handle":"marcelkargul","reposted":false,"text":"for context this is just a quick idea on how they could simplify the platform \n\ncompared to platforms like twitter and instagram, linkedin is insanely clunky to use in my opinion","created_at":"Sun Oct 11 20:11:54 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1791749514,"likes":7,"reposts":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"bookmarks":1,"views":2752,"is_note_tweet":false,"replying_to":{"screen_name":"marcelkargul","status":"2109370272017207487"},"quote":null,"media":null,"reposted_by":null},{"id":"2109273659038650501","url":"https://x.com/marcelkargul/status/2109273659038650501","author_handle":"marcelkargul","reposted":true,"text":"Lots of people in the comments keep saying to never use big negative letter spacing. I disagree. This is what I use with Geist:\n\n16px → 0%\n36px → -3%\n100px+ → -5 to -6%\n\nThe “never go negative” rule is for body text. At 100px+ the default spacing looks loose, because the gaps between letters scale up with the size. Tightening them is what makes big headlines look clean.\n\nBody text stays at 0%. The bigger the text, the tighter it gets. Nothing goes past -6%, because past that the letters start touching.","created_at":"Sun Oct 11 13:23:23 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1791725003,"likes":190,"reposts":6,"replies":12,"quotes":0,"bookmarks":178,"views":8685,"is_note_tweet":true,"replying_to":null,"quote":{"id":"2108984999345348785","text":"junior designer: Inter, Geist\n\nintermediate designer: Poppins, DM Sans, Instrument Sans\n\nsenior designer: Inter, Geist","author":"marcelkargul","media_n":1},"media":{"all":[{"type":"photo","width":3244,"height":4096,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUWkqlkW0AAJFmj.jpg?name=orig"}]},"reposted_by":true},{"id":"2109371241412858274","url":"https://x.com/marcelkargul/status/2109371241412858274","author_handle":"marcelkargul","reposted":false,"text":"talked to a founder who paid a 30+ person agency over $50k for a website redesign.\n\nit was absolute garbage.\n\nthis taught me that most really large agencies have junior designers doing the work while using 1 or 2 seniors on select projects.\n\nsmall focused teams with senior talent will almost always beat them.","created_at":"Sun Oct 11 19:51:08 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1791748268,"likes":104,"reposts":3,"replies":7,"quotes":4,"bookmarks":22,"views":7696,"is_note_tweet":true,"replying_to":null,"quote":null,"media":null,"reposted_by":null},{"id":"2109370272017207487","url":"https://x.com/marcelkargul/status/2109370272017207487","author_handle":"marcelkargul","reposted":false,"text":"ok when is linkedin getting a redesign?","created_at":"Sun Oct 11 19:47:17 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1791748037,"likes":160,"reposts":0,"replies":32,"quotes":7,"bookmarks":48,"views":39358,"is_note_tweet":false,"replying_to":null,"quote":null,"media":{"all":[{"type":"photo","width":2048,"height":1457,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUX9FHzXsAA5ZqA.jpg?name=orig"}]},"reposted_by":null},{"id":"2109273659038650501","url":"https://x.com/marcelkargul/status/2109273659038650501","author_handle":"marcelkargul","reposted":false,"text":"Lots of people in the comments keep saying to never use big negative letter spacing. I disagree. This is what I use with Geist:\n\n16px → 0%\n36px → -3%\n100px+ → -5 to -6%\n\nThe “never go negative” rule is for body text. At 100px+ the default spacing looks loose, because the gaps between letters scale up with the size. Tightening them is what makes big headlines look clean.\n\nBody text stays at 0%. The bigger the text, the tighter it gets. Nothing goes past -6%, because past that the letters start touching.","created_at":"Sun Oct 11 13:23:23 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1791725003,"likes":190,"reposts":6,"replies":12,"quotes":0,"bookmarks":178,"views